# 7. Why `show ip interface brief` Doesn't Show the IPv6 Addresses

After configuring IPv6, you ran:

```text
show ip int br
```

and got:

```text
GigabitEthernet0/0.10  10.0.18.1
GigabitEthernet0/0.20  10.0.18.33
```

You might wonder:

> "Where are my IPv6 addresses?"

They're not missing.

`show ip interface brief` is showing the **IPv4 addresses**.

You need the IPv6-specific command:

```text
show ipv6 interface brief
```

This distinction is important:

```text
show ip interface brief
        ↓
      IPv4


show ipv6 interface brief
        ↓
      IPv6
```

