# 16. What This Output Proves

Your output gives us several useful conclusions:

| Observation             | What it means                               |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| `Gi0/0.10 [up/up]`      | VLAN 10 subinterface is operational         |
| `Gi0/0.20 [up/up]`      | VLAN 20 subinterface is operational         |
| `2001:DB8:1:1::1`       | IPv6 gateway configured for VLAN 10         |
| `2001:DB8:1:2::1`       | IPv6 gateway configured for VLAN 20         |
| `FE80::...`             | Link-local IPv6 address present             |
| `ipv6 unicast-routing`  | IPv6 routing enabled globally               |
| IPv4 addresses remain   | IPv4 has not been removed                   |
| OSPF neighbor is `FULL` | Existing IPv4 OSPF adjacency is operational |

