## The Main Takeaway From Your Lab

You started with:

```text
VLAN 10 → 10.0.18.1
VLAN 20 → 10.0.18.33
```

Then you added:

```text
VLAN 10 → 2001:db8:1:1::1/64
VLAN 20 → 2001:db8:1:2::1/64
```

and globally enabled:

```text
ipv6 unicast-routing
```

The verification then showed:

```text
Gi0/0.10
FE80::...
2001:DB8:1:1::1

Gi0/0.20
FE80::...
2001:DB8:1:2::1
```

So you've successfully demonstrated the lesson's core idea:

> **The existing IPv4 network remains in place, while IPv6 is added to the same VLAN gateway interfaces.**

And the most important new observation is that **IPv6 automatically gives the interfaces a link-local `FE80::` address in addition to the configured IPv6 address.** That `FE80::` address is the piece you should carry forward into the next IPv6 address-types lesson.

